Drop the files that are not part of the library

This removes what open-quickshare's core_lib carries besides the Rust
library itself, none of which Sukkula builds or ships: the TypeScript
bindings and their build output (bindings/, dist/, esm/, package.json,
package-lock.json, tsconfig.json), the example programs (examples/), the
command-line demo (src/bin.rs, its [[bin]] target, and the dependencies
only it used: tracing-subscriber and tokio's "rt-multi-thread" and "signal"
features), the cross-compilation settings (Cross.toml), the release
profile (which cargo ignores for a dependency), upstream's Cargo.lock (the
embedding workspace's lockfile pins every dependency; one appears here
only when the crate is tested on its own, hence the .gitignore line), and
the rustfmt.toml, whose `group_imports` needs nightly rustfmt and only
makes stable `cargo fmt` warn.

No code of the library changes. This keeps the vendored tree to what is
reviewed and built, so that ci/vendor-check.sh and the patches that follow
are about the library alone.
